# What a target can't draw yet of what the gallery uses: the target, then the
# element as compiler/language/targets.hpp names it, a line each. The gallery's test
# fails while this differs from what's so, so it only ever gets shorter; a new
# target starts with everything here and is done when none of its lines are left.
# A terminal draws no pictures, so it can't show one alone, on a card or a table's
# row, crop one in place, match a collage's colors, or copy, save or keep a picture of
# a collage, and it has no screen of its own to take a screenshot of. A paper is
# written on in place, which a terminal doesn't do yet.
terminal cards.picture
terminal picture
terminal collage.copy
terminal collage.crop
terminal collage.match_colors
terminal collage.preview
terminal collage.save
terminal collage.screenshot
terminal table.picture
terminal paper
terminal paper.insert
terminal paper.outline
terminal paper.warm
terminal paper.spread
terminal paper.read_only
terminal paper.size
